For LSU6q22, you need to re-specifcy your exonic targets. Currently it’s every single loci as a target.

For the other, it seems there’s something wrong with your bam header. This part of the code, which leads to the error, is not part of CODEX — it only feeds into CODEX. Although I have to say this part has also been used by us and many other users so it shouldn’t be the script but rather the bam files. Can you try the following two things as a sanity check? (1) change *.bam.bai to *.bai only and rerun the code. I remember we talked about this solution while at ASHG. (2) can you make sure chr is of the same format in your code/bed file as well as in the bam file?

Hope this is of help,
Yuchao

