Hi Kirsten,

For LSU6q22, I think it’s solved — you need to respecify your targets.

For the other, sorry I wish I could be of more help but like I said, this part of the code is from the dependent package to get the read depth from the bam files. This has been used by a wide user base including myself with no problem. It seems something is wrong with you bams or bam headers. See https://www.biostars.org/p/54043/ . I would suggest reassemble your bams using the same pipeline as the one you used for the samples that turned out to work. If the problem persists, you need to contact the developer for Rsamtools instead of us. Another way to go around is to generate the read count matrix R using samtools in Linux instead of Rsamtools, although I feel you may have the same issue.

Yuchao

